2. PRESERVE THE CANONICAL ENTRY STRATEGY

Use the existing canonical Ekalayava entry logic as the baseline:

1. Process completed five-minute option candles chronologically.
2. Mark the Opening High and Opening Low from the first completed five-minute candle.
3. Require the premium to break below the Opening Low.
4. Detect the subsequent recovery or reversal structure using only information available at the time.
5. Identify the eligible causal swing high.
6. Enter at the completed candle close when the premium breaks the eligible swing high before reaching the Opening High.
7. Preserve the existing rule that the entry candle may close below the Opening High.
8. Match the exact contract, expiry and timestamps.

Do not use future candles to qualify entries or make stop/target decisions.

Do not change the entry logic merely to improve backtest performance. If you identify a specific weakness, create a separate experimental variant and evaluate it independently against the unchanged baseline.

